  "question": {
    "text": "A particle executes simple harmonic motion with a time period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;- axis.&nbsp;At time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, the particle crosses the mean position while at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, the&nbsp;velocity of the particle is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The amplitude of motion (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TSGJ2",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>π</mi></math>",
